@startuml smbus-overall
' Overall scenario -- the SMBus transactions the driver issues across a
' realistic lifecycle: probe/init, then a one-shot raw read, then setting a
' threshold. Zoomed out to one segment per transaction (no bit-level SCL).
title SMBus transactions across a lifecycle\nprobe -> one-shot raw read -> set threshold
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
scale 1 as 16 pixels

concise "Operation" as OP
concise "SMBus txn" as TX
robust "PWR_MODE (0x12)" as PWR

@0
OP is "Probe / init" #LightCyan
TX is "RD WHO_AM_I"
PWR is SLEEP
@6
TX is "RD CAL"
@12
TX is "WR CFG"
@18
TX is "WR INT_CFG"
@24
TX is "WR TH_LOW"
@30
TX is "WR TH_HIGH"
@36
OP is "One-shot raw read" #Wheat
TX is "WR PWR_MODE"
@40
PWR is "ONE-SHOT"
@42
TX is "RD STATUS"
@48
TX is "RD ALS"
@52
PWR is SLEEP
@54
OP is "Set threshold" #PaleGreen
TX is "WR TH_HIGH"
@60
OP is {hidden}
TX is {hidden}
@62

highlight 0 to 36 #F4FBFF : provision registers
highlight 36 to 54 #FFFBF4 : measure
highlight 54 to 60 #F4FFF4 : reconfigure
@enduml
